Vendored QuickBMS compression codecs
====================================

Source : quickbms-src-0.12.0.zip  (https://aluigi.altervista.org/quickbms.htm)
         src/compression/ and src/extra/ from that archive.

These files are the upstream QuickBMS codec sources, imported verbatim except
for #include path adjustments so they build outside the QuickBMS tree
(e.g. "../extra/mem2mem.h" -> "mem2mem.h").  They are compiled into the
wszst / wbmsx binaries and reached through ../qbms-comp.c, which the native
BMS interpreter (src/lib-bms.c) calls for COMTYPE / CLOG directives naming
one of these algorithms.

QuickBMS is licensed GPL-2.0, the same licence as this project.  Individual
codec files additionally carry their original authors' notices; those are
preserved in each file's header.  Nothing here changes the licensing of the
combined work, which remains GPL-2.0.

Files
-----
  mem2mem.c/.h        Luigi Auriemma  -- in-memory stdio shim used by splay.c
  lzss.c              Haruhiko Okumura LZSS (configurable window)
  lzari.c             Haruhiko Okumura LZARI (LZSS + arithmetic coding)
  lzhuf.c             Haruhiko Okumura LZHUF (LZSS + adaptive Huffman)
  unlzx.c             Amiga LZX archive stream decoder
  undmc.c             DMC (dynamic Markov compression) decoder
  unq3huff.c          Quake III adaptive Huffman decoder
  unshrink.c          PKWARE "shrink" (LZW) decoder
  yuke_bpe.c          Yuke's byte-pair-encoding decoder
  splay.c             CompressLib splay-tree decoder
  fastlz.c/.h         FastLZ (Ariya Hidayat)
  lzfx.c/.h           LZF-derived "lzfx"
  lzmat_dec.c/lzmat.h LZMAT decoder (Vitaly Evseenko)
  lz4x.c              LZ4X (small LZ4-compatible coder, Ilya Muravyov)
  Shrinker.c/.h       Shrinker LZ (Sergey Lyubka)
  smaz.c/.h           SMAZ short-string compressor (Salvatore Sanfilippo)
  sixpack.c           SIXPACK LZ + adaptive Huffman (Philip G. Gage)
  unlzw.c             Unix compress(1) / LZW_lib .Z-style LZW decoder
  unlzwx.c            LZWX variable-width LZW decoder
  qbms_lzh8.c         Nintendo LZH8 decoder (upstream lzh8_dec.c; entry point
                      renamed qbms_analyze_LZH8 to avoid clashing with the
                      FILE*-based analyze_LZH8 in src/lzh8_dec.c)
  scexpand.c          SCPACK byte-pair "strexpand" decoder (Star Control style)
  refpack.c           EA RefPack (10 FB) safe decoder

To add another upstream codec: copy its .c/.h here, fix includes so it
builds standalone, then add a prototype + table row + run_codec() case in
../qbms-comp.c.  The Makefile picks up new files in this directory
automatically.
